WEBVTT

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:25.860
How can I tell you this?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:36.970
How can I tell you this?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:47.620
I cannot touch you

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.230
But I...

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.860
...can kill you

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:05.570
I'm so sad to say to you...

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.600
...but don't put your face so close to me

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.020
Now I hear you say my name...

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:25.050
...so I cross the light to be with you

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:51.580
When We were Fish.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.490
Mitsuki...

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.670
At night, the sky is reflected in the pool...

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.860
...so it's like swimming in
outer space, don't you think?

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.950
I suppose the fish are always
exploring outer space...

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.250
...in search of water, just like this.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.610
Yeah.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.710
A ghost?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.110
Mitsuki Asano.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.610
How do you know my name?

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.050
You are going to die.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.720
So, you'd better live life to its fullest.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.210
Pardon?

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.550
Be seeing you.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.390
A-Asano?

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.860
Yutaka Fujishima? What are you doing here?

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.310
What about you?!

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.430
Not so loud. The security guard will spot us.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.910
Anyway, what are you doing here?

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.410
Listen, did you see a girl here a second ago?

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.650
A girl?

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:38.090
She was dressed in white. And she had a cat.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.150
Did you see them floating over there?

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.420
Are you feeling all right?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.160
Then what did I see?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.800
There's something more important. Listen...

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:48.890
What is it?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.730
I just let her go...

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.140
...in the pool.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.310
Let what go?

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.640
Uh, I'd rather not say. Anyway...

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.240
...I really think you should get out
of that pool quick.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.410
I plan to, eventually. What are you talking about?

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.350
I'm trying to tell you that I put "Pira" in the pool.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.290
Pira?

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.280
I put a piranha in the pool!

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.460
For real?

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.630
For real.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.410
Hey, I heard that swimming is canceled today.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.100
Really? That's awesome. I hate swimming.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.910
Why is swimming canceled?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.010
I heard that some idiot put a piranha in the pool.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.550
Good! Here it comes!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.190
Asano...

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:48.590
Is it true that you quit the basketball team?

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.100
Uh, yeah.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.670
But why? You were even in the team line-up.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.340
I didn't really have a reason.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.700
What a waste!

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.350
<i>GINGA BUN</i>
<i>Yakisoba Bun</i>

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.190
Oh...

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.150
Hey!

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.480
I don't think so!

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.630
This is mine.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.160
I saw it first.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.030
Here.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.400
Come again.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.130
Hey...

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.120
Hey, Asano.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.030
Go to the Science room after you're done.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.640
The teacher wants us to set up
the experiment before 5th period.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:35.940
Right.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.780
Boy, am I glad that I wasn't put
in charge of the science room.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.110
How come?

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.950
Fujishima would probably bite my head off.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.140
She scares me for some reason.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.040
You think so?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.120
Science
Room

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.120
About last night...

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.360
Rat me out if you want to. I don't care either way.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.190
I won't tell.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.870
Fine, if that's what you want to do.
It doesn't matter to me anyway.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.700
Where did you get the piranha from, anyway?

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.210
It's my dad's thing.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:14.240
We have aquariums all over the house.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.710
I feel like I'm living inside an aquarium.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.840
I draw the line at piranhas.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.290
Uh...

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.720
What?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.230
No, it's just that I thought you might
call your dad something derogatory...

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.660
...like "stupid old man".

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.000
I thought it was kind of refreshing
to hear you say "dad".

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.400
I'm not trying to mock you.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.960
Oh, be quiet.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.330
At least you call him "Dad".

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.570
You see, until elementary school...

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.680
...I called him "Daddy" in English.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.510
Seriously?

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.450
He trained me to call him that
as a joke, and Subaru...

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:01.590
...my big sister also called him that,
so I had no clue that something wasn't right.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.200
You, Asano?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.340
You were trained, like a kid in the boonies?

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.270
Oh, be quiet! Excuse me
for being an impressionable kid!

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:15.330
I should remind you that technically
we are in the boonies.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:18.100
Aw, I wish I never mentioned it.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.080
I can't help it...

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.510
Daddy?

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.940
Fine, laugh if you want to.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.990
It's too funny!

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.120
Did I get on your nerves?

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.260
You know...

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.750
...you're kind of pretty when you smile.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:50.800
So, how are you going to
get swimming canceled this time?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.070
Oh, there are many ways to get it done.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.540
I can always empty the pool.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.810
Do you really hate swimming that much?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.850
Kind of.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.550
All the girls seem to despise it.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.260
What is it?

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.350
I just heard a bell.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.460
Oh, it's probably that.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.790
See? On the Staff Room.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.440
ASANO

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.470
Big Sister Subaru...

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.020
Big Sister!

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.020
Mitsuki, you came to get me!

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.650
Yeah!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.370
How do you feel?

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.670
What are you guys?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.080
Hey, Human!

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.780
Momo went out of her way to come here...

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.750
...so show some respect!

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:08.610
Momo?

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:13.030
Yes. I am Reaper, Number 100100.

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:14.750
REAPER

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.750
But you can call me "Momo."

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.400
Reaper?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.900
Yes.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:18.930
Impossible.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.400
It's true!

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.870
If I can see a Reaper...

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.570
...does that mean I'm going to die?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:27.730
I said as much.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.300
When?

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:37.680
Good question. You're not quite there yet.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.920
I see. So, it's finally my turn.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.360
Hey...

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.130
You seem to have this odd belief...

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.460
...that you should have died
in someone else's place.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.460
You need to rethink that.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:54.890
What?

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.590
No one can take anyone else's place.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.170
That fate belongs to that person.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.670
Don't conveniently call it "fate".

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.840
Subaru was so much smarter than me...

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:11.810
...she was an athlete swimmer,
everyone had hope in her...

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.380
...she was so healthy...

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.880
...and she died so soon.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:21.220
Fate is defined as the carrying out of life.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:26.820
It doesn't change as long as you live,
and no one can take your place.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:32.000
If people could take over fate,
what fun would that be?

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:32.000
"I'M GOING TO BE HOSPITALIZED TOMORROW.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.000
Did we meet once before?

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.910
We did, at the pool last night.

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:44.180
No, not that. Somewhere, a long time ago.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.010
You're imagining things.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.990
Well, good luck.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.900
Good luck with what?

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.980
Big Sister...

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:27.430
Mitsuki, let's go to the pool...
at night again sometime.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.410
Mitsuki, I said come on down. It's dinner time.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.880
I'm opening the door.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.050
Honestly, what are you doing?

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:03.650
First you quit basketball, and
then you spend every day in a daze.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.160
But I guess you've always been a dreamer.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.140
'Cause Subaru really had her act together.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.140
Come on. We're having
your favorite tonight. Hamburg Steak.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.780
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:28.850
I'll be joining her...

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.250
...soon.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:41.160
You know, Asano, I'm kind of jealous of you.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:44.630
What do you mean?

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:48.300
It's like you're free to be yourself.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:53.510
Like you have your own mind.
I dunno, something like that.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.700
But aren't you the same?

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.550
I'm putting on a show. It's all fake.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.880
I'm just acting as though
I'm free to do as I please.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.190
I'd like to be more like you.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.870
No one can take anyone else's place.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.200
Huh?

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.540
It's nothing.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.800
Asano...

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.800
...since it's summer now,
is there somewhere you'd like to go?

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.740
Somewhere?

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:30.140
Um, like to the beach or to a pool?

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:34.050
But do you even go swimming ever?

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:37.720
Um, it doesn't have to be those places...

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.160
I guess it could be anywhere.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.330
Then summer has nothing to do with it.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.520
No, you're missing the point...

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.620
...I want to go somewhere with you.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.470
Hey, does that mean?

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.480
...that you like me?

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.710
Yeah, as if.

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.320
Is this for real?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:12.180
Apparently.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.190
What's so great about me?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.320
What's your favorite food?

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.430
What brought that on?

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.990
Go on, tell me.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.000
Hamburg Steak, I guess.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.310
That kind of suits you.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.380
Excuse me for being childish.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.740
Why do you like Hamburg Steak?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.540
Uh... because it's good?

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.190
Okay, then that's why.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:40.780
Excuse me?

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:44.320
Listen...

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.790
Huh?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.360
I'm going to die soon.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:08.210
If you don't like me, that's fine.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:12.850
But you don't have to mock me
with such a stupid joke.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.920
You don't have to mock how I feel.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.330
Oh, boy. You made her cry.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:28.200
Hey, Momo? Are these good?

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.070
I wouldn't, if I were you.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:31.800
You think?

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.810
Why did you come here?

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.940
Are you paying for your death with her tears?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.640
No. But why does it have to be me?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.520
If only it wasn't me...

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:51.460
...I could have told her whether I like her or not.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:54.390
Why can't it be you?

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.290
Because I'm going to...

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.200
Just tell her you like her.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.170
How could I?

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.830
I'm about to die, aren't I?

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.870
Maybe, but you're not the only one.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.510
That's why I wished you good luck.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.980
Don't try to encourage me. You're a Reaper.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:20.510
Your sister asked me to keep an eye on you.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.250
See you.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.500
Excuse me.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:32.700
Yes?

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.390
I'm Asano from 3-C.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.560
I'm not feeling well. May I lie down?

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.930
Did you get permission
from your home room teacher?

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:43.380
Yes.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.440
There's someone else here, so keep it quiet.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.180
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.750
Asano? You cut class.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:00.710
Is that you, Fujishima?

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.290
You cut class too.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.460
Listen, it doesn't bother me.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.360
You don't have to worry about it.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.060
I think I do love you...

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:19.880
...yeah, that's all. So, don't worry.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.340
It doesn't matter if you don't like me...

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.570
...or just think nothing of me at all.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.490
What? Are you feeling better already?

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:34.430
Nurse's
Office

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.360
Yes, thank you.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:37.120
ASANO

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.300
The ancient memory of when
human beings were once fish...

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.700
...lingers somewhere in our bodies.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:50.940
That is why we like to swim.

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:38.120
Asano, are you okay?

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.460
Fujishima? Why?

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.520
I couldn't help it! You weren't coming up at all!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:54.030
Wait, I thought you hated water?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.880
That's not really true...

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.380
What?

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.040
When I thought you were
going to die, I got so scared.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:05.120
I'm so glad!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.950
I'm so glad you're alive.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.080
I should have just told her.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.390
I wish I had taken Subaru's hand...

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:22.500
...and told her I would go with her again.

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:27.570
But it's kind of like... I don't want to die, y'know?

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:32.610
I couldn't take part in school activities like her...

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.440
...and my grades aren't as good
as hers either, but I...

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.540
...I want to live.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:44.620
Do you think he'll change?

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:47.020
Who knows? We'll see.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:53.300
And she told you that you were going to die?

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.320
Yeah, that's what she said.

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:57.800
When?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.640
Come to think of it, she never said when.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.970
Then we're the same.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:07.540
Nobody really knows when they're going to die.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.250
You're right. Everyone keeps on living...

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.450
...even though they know
they're going to die some day.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:16.080
Exactly.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.450
Living and carrying on life.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:39.040
I am going to carry away your
big sister's soul, okay?

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.210
No, don't take Subaru away.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:45.810
I have to.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.250
I'll go with her!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:52.220
No. You have to live your life.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:55.860
Live your life.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:01.600
That sound!

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.200
It's the Reaper.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:04.170
What?!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.130
Subaru...

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.000
...I'll be okay.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.640
Are you sympathy crying again?

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:26.760
Honest to God, Momo, you are such a crybaby.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:28.990
Oh, be quiet.

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:33.800
You go around visiting people
who aren't scheduled to die yet.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.330
What's so bad about that?

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:39.760
I think you're a total busybody.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.210
That's true.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:45.140
But that's who I am.

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:07.720
Fujishima.

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:17.300
I felt like swimming too.

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:21.310
Yeah.

00:22:49.770 --> 00:22:55.410
Fukai nemuri kara umareta

00:22:55.910 --> 00:23:03.550
Watashi naze namida tomaranai darou

00:23:05.060 --> 00:23:12.930
Shiroi kami nabiku yasashii kaze

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:19.830
Kotoba hitotsu, hitotsu omoi tsutau

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:30.620
Watashi no mune de ikutsumo no inochi

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:37.950
Hakanaku itoshiku keshite ku

00:23:38.460 --> 00:23:46.830
Yozora ni takaku shiroku mai odoru

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:55.070
Kono hitomi sorasazu mimamoru

00:23:59.980 --> 00:24:01.940
Next Episode

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:01.940
This is our final game.

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:05.780
I will travel past the distant sunlight to find it.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:08.650
Next episode: "Beyond the Light."

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:13.260
This is the sad and sweet story
of a white Reaper.

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:14.890
Beyond the Light.
